When one of the items of a wrapping column flex container has an aspect
ratio, Ladybird sizes them all in the width of the widest item’s
max-content contribution before it measures the container’s lines.
Blink also takes its items’ intrinsic contributions first, in its
FlexLayoutAlgorithm::ComputeMinMaxSizeOfMultilineColumnContainer().
Gecko’s nsFlexContainerFrame::ComputeIntrinsicISize() takes the largest
contribution for a column container. And WebKit establishes the items’
widths first, before it measures the lines, in its FlexLayout::
maximumContentSizeForMultilineColumn().
